1
00:00:00,072 --> 00:00:01,502
(Leonard:)I know, and I'm
proud of you,

2
00:00:01,507 --> 00:00:03,337
(Leonard:)but that doesn't mean I
can't do something nice.

3
00:00:03,342 --> 00:00:06,372
(Howard:)Like this.

4
00:00:06,378 --> 00:00:08,378
(Penny:)Okay, I don't want this
to turn into a fight.

5
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:09,510
(Leonard:)I don't, either.
Great.

6
00:00:09,515 --> 00:00:11,345
(Leonard:)Thank you.

7
00:00:14,186 --> 00:00:16,086
(Penny:)Can you pass the salt, please?
Sure.

8
00:00:22,361 --> 00:00:25,331
(Leonard:)In my mind, that broke
the tension with comedy

9
00:00:25,331 --> 00:00:27,201
(Leonard:)and led to sex.

10
00:00:28,534 --> 00:00:31,064
(clears throat)

11
00:00:32,371 --> 00:00:34,501
(Raj:)Hey, Sheldon, you busy?

12
00:00:34,507 --> 00:00:36,507
(Sheldon:)I'm always busy.

13
00:00:36,509 --> 00:00:39,709
(Sheldon:)This mind is capable
of advanced multitasking.

14
00:00:39,712 --> 00:00:40,682
(Sheldon:)You know, currently,

15
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:42,009
(Sheldon:)I'm attempting to solve

16
00:00:42,014 --> 00:00:43,344
(Sheldon:)the Penrose conjecture,

17
00:00:43,349 --> 00:00:45,919
(Sheldon:)I'm composing
my Nobel acceptance speech

18
00:00:45,918 --> 00:00:48,448
(Sheldon:)for when I've solved
the Penrose conjecture,

19
00:00:48,454 --> 00:00:51,484
(Sheldon:)and I'm wondering
how mermaids have babies.

20
00:00:52,892 --> 00:00:55,462
(Raj:)Don't they lay eggs on a rock?

21
00:00:56,896 --> 00:00:59,296
(Sheldon:)Now I've got room
for another thing.

22
00:00:59,298 --> 00:01:00,768
(Sheldon:)What do you want?

